---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/hugin.css';
---

<Layout>

  <main class="hugin-page">

    <section class="hugin-hero">
      <div class="hugin-heading">
        <a class="back-link" href="/projects">← Projects</a>

        <p class="hugin-label">
          01 · Embedded systems · Home automation
        </p>

        <h1 class="hugin-title">Hugin</h1>

        <p class="hugin-intro">
          A local-first room sensor platform combining presence and
          environmental sensing in a single device.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hugin-meta">
        <div>
          <span>Platform</span>
          <strong>ESP32-C6</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>Integration</span>
          <strong>ESPHome · Home Assistant</strong>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>Status</span>
          <strong>Prototype</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>


    <section class="story-section">
      <div class="story-heading">
        <span>Overview</span>
        <h2>
          One platform.<br />
          Multiple sensors.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="story-copy">
        <p>
          Hugin is built around an ESP32-C6 and ESPHome, bringing several
          sensors together in one device. Their data is exposed to Home Assistant,
          where it can be used for dashboards and automations.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="story-section">
      <div class="story-heading">
        <span>Motivation</span>
        <h2>
          Why I built it.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="story-copy">
        <p>
          I wanted a single room sensor that could combine several functions
          instead of relying on separate devices for each one. I could not find
          an off-the-shelf multisensor that matched what I had in mind, so I
          decided to build one myself.
        </p>

        <p>
          That also means I can choose exactly which sensors to use, keep the
          system local and change the hardware as the project develops. Along the
          way, I am learning more about embedded development, sensor integration
          and hardware prototyping.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="architecture-section">
      <div class="architecture-heading">
        <span>Architecture</span>
        <h2>From room data<br />to automation.</h2>

        <p>
          Hugin sends presence and environmental data to Home Assistant
          through ESPHome.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="architecture-flow">
        <div class="architecture-node">
          <span class="node-number">01</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Local sensors</strong>
            <p>Presence and environmental data</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="architecture-connector" aria-hidden="true">
          <span></span>
        </div>

        <div class="architecture-node architecture-node-primary">
          <span class="node-number">02</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Hugin</strong>
            <p>ESP32-C6 · ESPHome</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="architecture-connector" aria-hidden="true">
          <span></span>
        </div>

        <div class="architecture-node">
          <span class="node-number">03</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Home Assistant</strong>
            <p>Data · dashboards · automations</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="status-section">
      <div class="status-heading">
        <span>Current status</span>

        <h2>
          Prototype now.<br />
          Permanent hardware next.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="status-content">
        <div class="status-state">
          <span class="status-dot"></span>
          <div>
            <small>Current phase</small>
            <strong>Prototyping & testing</strong>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="status-steps">
          <div class="status-step">
            <span>01</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Prototype</strong>
              <p>
                Develop and test the ESP32-C6 platform, sensors and
                Home Assistant integration.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="status-step">
            <span>02</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Permanent build</strong>
              <p>
                Move from a breadboard prototype to hardware I can
                install in a room.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="status-step">
            <span>03</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Custom hardware</strong>
              <p>
                Explore a dedicated PCB and enclosure once the sensor
                configuration has been validated.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a
          class="github-link"
          href="https://github.com/Pdoxxy/hugin"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >
          View Hugin on GitHub
          <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</Layout>
